The block outputs noise corrupted versions of the input position, velocity, and orientation. Specify additional kinematics to simulate noise-corrupted acceleration and angular velocity. Simulate GNSS loss by specifying a position error factor.

Vary the Roll, Pitch, Yaw, Position and Velocity accuracies to change the noise levels present in the output signals. Accuracy is defined as the standard deviation of the noise.

The Position and Velocity input ports should be N-by-3 vectors. The Orientation input port should be an N-by-4 quaternion array, a 3-by-3-by-N array of rotation matrices, or an N-by-3 array of Euler angles in degrees.</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/INS</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/INS</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>240  337  415  453</block_position><block_icon>INS.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:3,signal.out_signal:3</port_domains><block_type>MATLABSystem</block_type><block_reference>sensorinslib/INS</block_reference></block_node><block_node SID="31" hasTree="0"><block_name>Bicycle Model - Velocity Input</block_name><block_class>Vehicle Body 3DOF Lateral</block_class><block_desc>autoblks_shared:autoblkVehBody3DofADTx:blkDesc</block_desc><block_path>$bdroot/Bicycle Model - Velocity Input</block_path><block_open>$bdroot/Bicycle Model - Velocity Input</block_open><block_isNotLeafBlk>0</block_isNotLeafBlk><block_position>460  340  665  500</block_position><block_icon>Bicycle@20@Model@20@@2D@@20@Velocity@20@Input.svg</block_icon><keywords></keywords><port_domains>signal.in_signal:2,signal.out_signal:5</port_domains><block_type>SubSystem</block_type><block_reference>autolibshared/Bicycle Model - Velocity Input</block_reference></block_node></library>